 ## Test Design Principles
 
 ### One Behavior Per Test
 
-Each test should verify exactly one behavior. This makes failures easy to diagnose and tests easy to maintain.
+Keep each test focused on a coherent behavior. Multiple assertions may establish
+one outcome or state transition; assertion count is not a quality gate. Avoid
+splitting an interaction so far that its important contract disappears.
 
